WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:07.059 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  my best friend in high school was Shawn  we would sit together every day launch  skip classes on Fridays to go on a  weekend adventure and surround ourselves  with Weidman snacks when we were  collaborating on our homework  Shawn would carry mathematically gifted  and super cute evidenced by all the  girls would ask me to deliver love  letters in card to him however deep in  his heart he was depressed he was deeply  upset by his parents longtime fights he  was feeling suffocated by the  unrealistically high expectations of his  parents and I was the only person that  he trusted to share his true feelings  with one day after school I bumped into  Shawn's mom I really wanted to alert her  to John suffering but I was afraid the  speaking the truth would embarrass her  and Shan Shan  so I remained silent after high school  Shawn and I went to different colleges  but we stayed in touch then one cold  winter night the second night after 2014  Chinese New Year I received a picture  message from Shawn he had written  happy New Year to me on a frost covered  window then I receive a call from him I  picked up and said thank you so much  Shawn this is so sweet  happy New Year to you as well but what I  heard was Shawn crying uncontrollably  he said that he didn't know how to be  happy in the new year he told me that he  couldn't see a way out of his pain and  he wanted to terminate his suffering  before I could respond I heard some  weird noises and then just silence my  heart froze and my mind went blank Shawn  had jumped out the window of his dorm  I remember how painful it was waiting  outside of Shawn's ICU when a Herschel  parents condemned himself for not  recognizing his fragile mental state I  realized that he had never spoken to his  parents about his suffering and neither  had I when I had the opportunity fear  and doubt kept me silent for three days  I picked my eyes on Shawn's harm on her  screen all of sudden the heart beat  pattern came to a freefall  and turning to a flatline I will always  remember the moment of silence when I  felt so devastated when I realized what  the cause of silence could be  I know this is an extreme case but  perhaps you can relate  perhaps there's been a time in your life  that you've been silent because of your  fear of speaking up at work with friends  in relationship because silence seemed  like the safer choice the silence has  caused where you fail to stand up for  your beliefs you may later feel like  you've lost a part of yourself  and miss out on giving a voice to others  who may feel the same when you hide a  part of your identity for the fear of  not being accepted you may suffer from  never leaving fully and lack a true  sense of belonging when you choose not  to share your true feelings with someone  really care about you may miss out on  potentially beautiful relationship we  tend to think that maintainence does  close safe while making changes is risky  so we're often focused on analyzing the  cause of speaking up without even  considering the cause of silence even I  who have paid such a high price to  understand the cost still found myself  being silent about things that mattered  two years ago on the outside I seem to  have it all I was on a promising career  track with the boyfriend who checked all  the boxes and I would live in Hong Kong  and exciting  new city but the truth was I was very  unhappy in my job my boyfriend's  critical comments always made me feel  inferior and never good enough and for  the first time in my life I was living  by myself with no support group around  me on the inside I felt sad and alone  whenever my parents asked me how I was  doing  I wanted to tell them the truth but I  couldn't I couldn't because I was afraid  to shatter the illusion of my perfect  life I was afraid that something better  didn't exist for me so for nearly a year  I silenced myself and it was painful one  night I lay in bed in complete darkness  I felt hopeless I couldn't see a way out  then suddenly all my memories of Shawn  flooding my mind I thought about his  suffering in silence in the moment when  I lost him forever  and I was reminded of the ultimate cost  of silence  it was at this moment that I decided on  a shelf memory by breaking my own  silence by taking the staff that he was  now able to take I share my frustrations  and my fears with my parents and I was  surprised to find that my being real in  front of them felt so much better than  my trying to be the perfect child and  instead of feeling secure I felt a  stronger sense of love and belonging by  sharing my truth rather than hiding it  and struggling to maintain illusion with  my parent support I end the relationship  and apply to the new school and look at  me now this isn't to say that things are  always perfect but trust me they're so  much better I have found my voice I mean  breaking new possibilities and deeper  more meaningful relationships if I had  remained silent two years ago I would  have shut myself off from everything I'm  experiencing now acknowledging the code  of silence was a wake-up call for me I  learned it the hard way and I don't want  you to have to go through anything  similar my greatest hope is that you can  recognize those moments when a cop  speaking up may seem high but the cup of  silence is even greater and that you use  your voice to prevent yourself from  never knowing what my husband have just  spoken up  what are you currently being silent  about what are you not expressing them I  open up new possibilities for you your  relationship with others and perhaps  more importantly in your relationship  with yourself I encourage you to find  your voice thank you  [Applause]  [Music]

